* ============================================================
*  LIMITS SHAKEDOWN -- CLOSE ALL over multiple work areas
*
*  Status:  CANDIDATE / REVIEW_BEFORE_EXECUTION.
*  Safety:  MUTATING on throwaway tables only (CATMP5/CATMP260/CATMP400),
*           ERASEd at the end. Touches no fixtures.
*  Proves:  The 2026-07-19 CLOSE ALL correction (src/cli/cmd_close.cpp) closes
*           EVERY open work area, not just the current one. Also exercises
*           MAX_AREA>256 by opening real tables in areas 260 and 400.
*
*  DISCRIMINATING OUTCOME
*  ----------------------
*    AFTER the fix : all three ERASE report "Deleted: 1, Failed: 0"
*                    (CLOSE ALL released every area's file handle).
*    BEFORE the fix: CATMP5 and CATMP260 (non-current areas) ERASE
*                    "FAILED ... being used by another process" and are stranded.
*
*  RUN
*  ---
*  DOTSCRIPT TRACE scripts\limits\limits_close_all_shakedown.dts OUT tmp\limits\close_all.log
* ============================================================
SET ECHO OFF
SET TALK ON

ECHO ############################################################
ECHO # CLOSE ALL SHAKEDOWN -- close every open work area
ECHO ############################################################

ECHO === C1. open a throwaway table in area 5 ===
SELECT 5
CREATE X64 CATMP5 (ID N(4))

ECHO === C2. open a throwaway table in area 260 (beyond old MAX_AREA=256) ===
SELECT 260
CREATE X64 CATMP260 (ID N(4))

ECHO === C3. open a throwaway table in area 400 ===
SELECT 400
CREATE X64 CATMP400 (ID N(4))

ECHO === C4. CLOSE ALL -> must close areas 5, 260, and 400 (not just current 400) ===
CLOSE ALL

ECHO === C5. ERASE each -> all must report Deleted: 1, Failed: 0 ===
ERASE CATMP5 CONFIRM
ERASE CATMP260 CONFIRM
ERASE CATMP400 CONFIRM

ECHO CLOSE-ALL SHAKEDOWN COMPLETE.
